From: superturtlee <160681686+superturtlee@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 22 Jun 2026 00:52:12 +0800
Subject: backend: add anland zero-copy display backend (ported from 15.0.90)

Add the anland backend, which provides a zero-copy display path via
shared DMA-BUFs and a Unix domain socket protocol to an external display
daemon (libdisplay_producer).

The backend was originally developed against Weston 15.0.90 and has been
adapted to the 14.0.2 API surface with the following changes:

  - Remove Vulkan renderer support (not available in 14.x).
  - Convert input notification calls from the 15.x event-struct API
    (weston_*_event_init + notify) to the 14.x direct-call API
    (notify_motion, notify_button, notify_key, notify_touch).
  - Replace weston_renderbuffer_t typedef with struct weston_renderbuffer *.
  - Adjust create_renderbuffer_dmabuf() call from 4 args to 2 args.
  - Replace renderer->destroy_renderbuffer() with weston_renderbuffer_unref().
  - Adjust weston_touch_create_touch_device() from 5 args to 4 args.

New files:
  - libweston/backend-anland/anland.c
  - libweston/backend-anland/meson.build
  - libweston/backend-anland/vendor/display_producer.c
  - libweston/backend-anland/vendor/display_producer.h
  - libweston/backend-anland/vendor/protocol.h
  - libweston/backend-anland/vendor/socket_utils.c
  - libweston/backend-anland/vendor/socket_utils.h
  - include/libweston/backend-anland.h

Based-on-patch: https://github.com/lfdevs/weston/commit/776599ab62a6dc8f6bb1d36c8b14ea354c190301

Co-authored-by: lfdevs <lfdevs@lfdevs.com>
